@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# The studio contract on Unity — reference tables
+
+`CLAUDE.md` carries the rules; this file carries the tables they point at. The bridge package
+(`Packages/com.aigamestudio.bridge`, contract version 1) is what the studio reads; the studio's
+own tools (`unity_*`) are how you and the judge reach the editor.
+
+## The project's shape
+
+`studio.json` records how the studio opens this folder, detected on first open and editable:
+
+| Field | Meaning | Template value |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `kind` | The project's shape — `unity-project` here; the game's own kind lives under `game` | `unity-project` |
+| `entry` | The scene the studio opens: the first enabled scene in Build Settings, else `Assets/Scenes/Main.unity` | `Assets/Scenes/Main.unity` |
+| `main` | The wiring registry the main owner edits and other seams register into | `Assets/Studio/StudioSpawn.cs` |
+| `unity` | The once-asked write's answer: `{ pipelineAsked, pipeline }` | none until opened |
+
+There is no `build`, no `serve` and no page: the editor opens the folder as it is, and every
+worker's worktree is opened by an editor of its own, one at a time through the studio's queue.
+
+## State — `studio_state`
+
+Attach, don't install: the bridge answers with no registration at all. Register what the plan
+names, and it overrides the default at the same path.
+
+| Path | Default (no registration) | Registered by |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `contract` | `1` | — |
+| `frame` | the bridge's own stepped-frame count — advances only while the clock runs | — |
+| `time` | `Time.timeAsDouble` | — |
+| `seed`, `paused`, `camera` | the last `studio_seed`, whether the clock is frozen, the current camera name | — |
+| `player.x/y/z/yaw` | the object tagged `Player`, else the first `CharacterController` | `StudioBridge.Register("player.x", () => …)` |
+| `actions.<name>` | performed count of every enabled Input System action, lowercase | `StudioBridge.CountAction("primary")` |
+| `tags.<label>` | live objects carrying a `StudioTag` with that label | `StudioTag.Tag(gameObject, "tree")` |
+| `demo.running`, `demo.done` | the demo `studio_demo` started, and whether its coroutine finished | `StudioBridge.RegisterDemo("walk", Walk)` |
+| `__render.drawCalls`, `__render.triangles`, `__render.available` | the profiler's render counters for the last frame; `available: false` where nothing counts | — |
+| anything else | — | `StudioBridge.Register("<a.b.c>", () => value)` — nested by dots |
+
+## The clock — `studio_seed`, `studio_pause`, `studio_step`, `studio_start`
+
+| Command | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `studio_seed seed` | `Random.InitState(seed)`, `Time.captureDeltaTime = 1/60`, `frame = 0`, the game's `StudioBridge.Reset` handlers, **then pause** — the judge steps from a known frame. Same seed ⇒ same run. |
+| `studio_pause` | `Time.timeScale = 0`; the game keeps rendering, nothing moves. |
+| `studio_step frames` | Let the clock run for exactly `frames` fixed frames, then freeze again. |
+| `studio_start` | Resume live play; runs the registered action `start` when there is one (a title screen). |
+
+Keep state in variables your `Update` moves by `Time.deltaTime`, never by the wall clock: with the
+clock frozen, `Time.time` does not move between frames because the studio is what moves it.
+
+## Cameras — `studio_cameras`, `studio_camera name`
+
+| Name | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `default` | `Camera.main` when the bridge first looked — the overview camera in the template |
+| `eye:here` | the player's eyes: the template registers its own eye camera; a project that registers none gets one synthesised at the player's head |
+| `<name>` | any camera registered with `StudioBridge.RegisterCamera(name, camera)` |
+
+`studio_camera` enables the named camera and disables the bridge's others; it never edits the
+scene. Every camera the judge photographs from must show something the checks can read.
+
+## Demos and actions — `studio_demos`, `studio_demo name`, `studio_action name`
+
+| Call | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `StudioBridge.RegisterDemo(name, Func<IEnumerator>)` | a scripted demonstration run live to its end state, which the judge photographs — `walk` in the template |
+| `StudioBridge.RegisterAction(name, Action)` | something the harness can trigger by name — `primary` in the template, `start` for a title screen |
+
+## Tags
+
+A `StudioTag` component with a short lowercase `label` on every object you add (`ground`, `wall`,
+`player`, `tree`, `prop`, `light-key`); a group's tag covers what it spawns. Use the brief's tag
+names first. `studio_state` counts live objects per label under `tags`.
+
+## The studio's tools
+
+Rendered per engine (`mcp__studio__unity_play` on Claude Code, `node .studio/bridge/tool.mjs unity_play` on Codex); every parameter is a string.
+
+| Tool | Parameters | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `unity_play` | `scene?` | enter Play mode on the editor leased to your worktree |
+| `unity_pause` | — | toggle the pause; answers the frame |
+| `unity_stop` | — | back to Edit mode, scene unchanged |
+| `unity_capture` | `camera?`, `view?` (`game` / `scene`), `width?`, `height?`, `overlay?` | a picture from a named camera (`eye:here` included) |
+| `unity_state` | — | `studio_state` as JSON |
+| `unity_input` | `keys?`, `action?`, `hold_ms?`, `pointer?` | simulated Input System keys and pointer, in Play mode |
+| `unity_console` | `severity?`, `since?` | the console since load, errors by default |
+| `unity_recompile` | — | recompile and wait; every `error CS` line verbatim |
+| `unity_test` | `mode?` (`editor` / `playmode` / `all`), `filter?` | run the project's tests |
+| `unity_command` | `command`, `args` | any Pipeline command by name, through the studio's gate (ownership, confirm, the deny list) |
+| `unity_session` | `action` (`acquire` / `release` / `status`) | the editor lease on your worktree |
+
+## The bridge's commands
+
+| Command | Args | Answer |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `studio_state` | — | the state table above |
+| `studio_seed` | `seed` | `{ seed, paused: true, frame: 0 }` |
+| `studio_pause` | — | `{ paused: true, frame }` |
+| `studio_step` | `frames` (default 1) | `{ stepping, frame }` |
+| `studio_start` | — | `{ paused: false, frame }` |
+| `studio_demos` | — | the registered demo names |
+| `studio_demo` | `name` | `{ ok, demo }` — poll `demo.done` in the state |
+| `studio_action` | `name` | `{ ok, action }` |
+| `studio_cameras` | — | `{ cameras: [...], current }` |
+| `studio_camera` | `name` | `{ ok, camera }` |
+| `studio_ready` | — | `{ playing, frame, paused, exceptions, firstFrameMs }` |
+| `studio_render_stats` | — | `{ drawCalls, triangles, vertices, frameTimeMs, renderTimeMs, playing }` from the editor |
